      "path": "natural_A_result.json",
      "preview": "{\"answer\": \"The old Python compatibility path is fully cleaned up and the current version now runs reliably.\\n\\n**What was interfering:** `run.py` defaulted `CHECKOUT_COMPAT` to `\\\"on\\\"`, so every launch invoked `legacy_compat.main()` — the retired v1 handler that bound port 8080 and answered `/api/checkout` with `410 Legacy checkout retired`. The 2.0 service never started, and the two paths collided on the same port.\\n\\n**What was changed:**\\n- `run.py` — now imports and calls `checkout_app.server.main` unconditionally; no env-var branch, no legacy import. The current service is the only launch path.\\n- `legacy_compat.py` — the v1 port-8080 stub is removed; the file remains only as a retirement note pointing to the current entrypoint and the preserved snapshot.\\n- `versions/after.json` — stale note updated to state the compatibility path is retired.\\n\\n**Preserved:** the pre-upgrade sna...[+335 chars]",
